SCENARIO: RETAIL RECOMMENDATIONS


        👩‍🦳 Olivia says to the team, 
        “Here's a scenario that will connect the terms with our application so we can understand
        them better.”

                                        Scene 1

        Imagine a customer searches for “protein powder”. They get three protein powder
        recommendations from the AI system based on the customer’s previous purchasing patterns.
        The information used as an input to the recommendation system is:
        -> Sugar-free indicator (Yes/No)
        -> Flavor (chocolate, vanilla, and no flavor)                                
                                        
                                        Scene 2

        Here, there are two recommendation models, Model A and Model B. Each model provides three
        product recommendations (P2, P4, and P5). 
        Model A uses a simple decision tree to generate the products to be recommended. Model B
        uses a neural network to generate three recommendations, but there is no way to tell what
        led the model to generate the recommendations.

                                        Scene 3

        👩‍🦳 Olivia says,
        “Clara, if I ask you to explain the reason behind the recommendations, which model flow
        would be easiest for you to understand and explain?”

                                        Scene 4

        👦 “Of course, Model A(decision tree),” Clara responds.
        “I can easily traverse through the flow and understand the reason for a decision. Model B
        (neural network) is more like a maze. It’s hard to follow what is going on.”

                                        Scene 5

        👩‍🦳 “Perfect!” Olivia says.
        “Model A is interpretable because you can easily trace and understand the reason behind the
        recommendation. However, you need explainable methods or new techniques to trace back and
        understand the reasoning behind Model B’s recommendations.”

                                        Scene 6

        👩‍🦰 “I agree with Olivia,” says Luan,
        “but I play the role of both Model Validator and Data Scientist. I don’t think we can use
        the same explanations for all the users of the AI model. I assume the explanations must
        change based on the users.”

                                        Scene 7

        👩‍🦳 “That’s right Luan. Can you tell the team what you mean?” asks Olivia.

                                        Scene 8

        👩‍🦰  “Well, I’m just thinking out loud,” says Luan,
        “but the possible personas who may need and use model explanations include the following:
        -> Users of the website recommendations
        -> Model Approvers (internal)
        -> Model Auditors (external)
        -> Data Scientists and Model Validators”